Published-source checks after unpacking those archives:
- `clap-4.6.6/Cargo.toml` declares `derive`, `env`, `string`, and `wrap_help`; its default feature list includes `suggestions`.
- `clap_builder-4.6.6/Cargo.toml` maps `suggestions` to `dep:strsim`, and declares `strsim = "0.11.1"` optional. The resolved tree enables the default and suggestions features and contains transitive `strsim v0.11.1`.
- `clap_complete-4.6.9/Cargo.toml` accepts clap `4.5.20` or later with `default-features = false`; its `Shell` enum contains Bash, Elvish, Fish, PowerShell, and Zsh, and `aot::generate` accepts `&mut dyn Write`.
- `clap_builder-4.6.6/src/parser/parser.rs:1322-1329` dispatches `ArgAction::Version` with `Identifier::Long => true` and `Identifier::Short => false`. `src/builder/command.rs:4898-4914` selects `long_version` for the long form and `version` for the short form, then renders `format!("{display_name} {ver}\\n")`.
- `src/builder/arg.rs:881-884` states that global arguments propagate down and may be used at any position; `:2205-2210` defines per-argument `Arg::env`.
- `src/parser/features/suggestions.rs:19-21` uses `strsim::jaro` and accepts confidence strictly greater than `0.7`.
- A recursive symbol search of the published `clap_builder-4.6.6` and `clap_derive-4.6.4` archives found no `env_prefix`, `auto_env`, or `envvar_prefix` symbol.

